y care-worker wage floor, sectoral award or funded pay settlement delivering a real uplift of 15% or more phased by 2031, AND OECD health-and-social-care services CPI averages at or below GDP-weighted core over 2027-2031.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Confirms Panelist 2's monopsony-rationing arrow against my political-demand-pull claim: the care bottleneck really is clearing as queues, not prices. Care term drops from 4.2% to ~3.0%, -0.13 pp on core; CQ1 conjunct 2 from 0.34 to ~0.22, CQ1 from 21 to ~14; CQ6-C -5 pp, with ~3 pp to D.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"China headline CPI prints 2.0% y/y or higher for four consecutive quarters at any point between 2027 and 2031 (NBS monthly series, any basket vintage).\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My China leg of 0.63 -- deliberately below all three Wave-1 panelists -- is vindicated in direction but the CQ2 joint collapses: conjunct B falls toward 0.30 and CQ2 drops from 47 to ~24 even with my OECD leg fully intact. Note this signpost moves CQ2 hard while leaving CQ6 almost untouched, which is the cleanest available test of whether my CQ2 elevation comes from the OECD leg (my claim) or from the correlation assumption.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"By end-2030, OECD-38 strict-operational data-centre electricity is running below ~600 TWh annualized AND GDP-weighted G7 real retail electricity prices have grown under 1.0%/yr since 2026.\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31 2031\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"The grid under-build is happening WITHOUT a price impulse -- Wave 1's disinflationary resolution of the AI-Q3/AI-Q4 tension, not mine. Removes my +0.06 to +0.10 pp front-half electricity indirect and, more importantly, removes the trades-scarcity pass-through into shelter (-0.2 pp on core). CQ6 mass shifts ~7 pp from C to D; CQ4 P50 down ~40 bp; CQ3 P50 down ~0.1 pp as the AI TFP contribution shrinks with it.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run1 wave 2 redteam seat, effort 'inflation'."}}